## Why This Task Exists

The native CLI is the Jury operator authority boundary, not a thin spelling of internal APIs. Routing every operation through the same guarded backend keeps automation and interactive use from bypassing policy, decrypting unrelated items, or leaking private values through structured output.

## Outcome

Expose native identity, witnessed-policy administration, provider-backed read/inject, transfer, backup, audit, and rollover through one guarded CLI use-case layer. J22 adds request, approve, receipt, and witnessed execution commands.

## Required Work

- Keep parsing and presentation thin; core crates own policy replay, authorization, cryptography, and atomic mutation.
- Provide role-specific identity create, inspect, rotate, replace, and protector commands for vault principals, approvers, and witnesses.
- Provide explicit witnessed governance commands, including policy require witnessed, eligible approver/witness membership, approval quorum, witness quorum, allowed operations, request lifetime, and workload limits.
- Require an authenticated acknowledgement for policy allow direct or any command that introduces a usable direct slot or weakens a witnessed requirement.
- Provide policy status and explain output that reports mode, satisfiable membership/quorum, pending-request invalidation, and direct-slot suppression without exposing private names.
- Route selected-item operations through ItemAccessProvider so witnessed-only items cannot acquire a direct fallback.
- Make repository, global, and explicit vault selection deterministic.
- Separate human output from bounded structured output and preserve committed-versus-retryable reporting.
- Never emit values, passphrases, keys, private names, or protected state to logs or errors.

## Required Tests

Cover command parsing and help, all role/membership/quorum/mode transitions, missing downgrade acknowledgement, selector ambiguity, hostile paths, structured-output bounds, inaccessible-name absence, repository trust states, atomic mutations, failure/cancellation, and secret-leak scans.

## Dependencies

