## Why This Task Exists

J26 is the single active release join. It prevents a direct-only build, stub witness service, receipt demonstration, or incomplete security corpus from being called the witnessed product, and it binds explicit externally-unreviewed pre-alpha language to the exact artifacts operators can build and rehearse.

## Outcome

A fresh operator can verify, build, configure witnessed governance, self-host, run, back up, and recover one exact experimental witnessed-access candidate while understanding that Jury has received no independent professional security review and is unsuitable for real secrets. J15 compatibility and J19R/J19D/J19E external-review work are not advertised as shipped.

## Required Work

- finalize license and trademark policy and publish format, slot, protocol, receipt, rollback-anchor, vector, upgrade, rollback, backup, recovery, incident-response, and security-reporting documentation;
- produce signed binaries, checksums, SBOM, provenance, and clean-environment reproducible build instructions bound to one exact candidate;
- segregate signing authority from ordinary CI; use a least-privileged offline, hardware-backed, or immutable keyless identity; record an explicit named solo-maintainer release decision and publish rotation, revocation, compromise-recovery, and trusted replacement-key procedures;
- dogfood witnessed-only request, meaningful approver decision, quorum contributions, read/inject/exec, receipt, next-revision denial, rotation, recovery, repo-local lifecycle, backup drill/restore, and rollover with generic data;
- disclose direct-slot unilateral access, endpoint retention, historical decryptability, offline freshness limits, metadata leakage, HNDL/PQ/FIPS/forward-secrecy nonclaims, and suite-migration boundaries;
- state prominently that no independent professional security review occurred and that J19R/J19D/J19E remain deferred optional work;
- self-review the exact candidate in a fresh pass and identify it honestly as self-review;
- from a clean checkout or equivalent clean worktree, rerun all release checks, conformance/adversarial suites, dependency/advisory checks, source/binary identity checks, and reproducible build commands;
- bind exact source, J19 manifest, verifier, provider lock data, build inputs, binaries, checksums, SBOM, and provenance; invalidate the release binding on any change;
- disposition every confirmed finding; unresolved medium-or-higher security findings block release;
- retain the pre-alpha, externally-unreviewed, and no-real-secrets warning throughout 0.x.

Models, coding agents, alternate implementations, automated tests, self-review, and clean rebuilds are engineering evidence. None is an independent reviewer.

